# Conventional Commits

All git commit messages in this repo MUST use Conventional Commits:

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`.

- Imperative, lowercase description, no trailing period, ≤72 char subject
- Do not copy non-conventional history (e.g. `Initial commit`)
- No gitmoji

When writing or suggesting a commit message, output only a valid conventional commit (subject + optional body).
